Hello,

I have a large multi-session dataset (see screenshot) where I want to calculate sigma and dectection by session. Some sessions were quite sparsely sampled, and in that case I’d like to be able to pool these to share estimates.

There are 42 sessions, and a few of them I would like to pool. For example 29:33 were all in the same place, just in different years, and sampling was low intensity (thus so were recaptures). I would like to pool these together and only estimate a single detection and sigma value across these, while estimating independent estimates across the other sessions.

I feel like this must be easy, but I went down a rabbit hole of complex coding and decided to step back and ask the experts!

Cheers,
Clayton

